Loupe's app shell. {{ entry.summary }}

```jsx
<{{ entry.name }}
  projectName="Acme"
  active="board"
  crumbs={['Acme', 'Board']}
  userName="riley@example.com"
>
  <h1>Board</h1>
</{{ entry.name }}>
```

Wrap every signed-in page in it. The sidebar and the top bar are part of the shell, so do not draw your own. The page content goes in as the children. Pass `meta` for a short line after the breadcrumb and `actions` for page buttons in the top bar. The New work button is always there.

`active` takes the name of a nav link. The wrapper holds the same links as the app, with the same labels. The component emits the real `{{ entry.rootClass }}`, `lp-sidebar`, `lp-topbar` and `lp-main` classes of the app.
{% endautoescape %}
